'''''Justicia carnea''''', the '''Brazilian plume flower''', '''Brazilian-plume''', '''flamingo flower''', or '''jacobinia''', is a [[flowering plant]] in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Acanthaceae]].<ref>{{PLANTS|id=JUCA17|taxon=Justicia carnea|accessdate=28 May 2015}}</ref>

The [[perennial plant]] is native to the [[Atlantic Forest]] [[ecoregion]]s of eastern [[Brazil]], [[Misiones Province]] of northeastern [[Argentina]], and [[Paraguay]].<ref name = powo/>

It is cultivated and sold as a decorative potted plant and is planted in landscaping as a feature plant in warm temperate and subtropical climates.

